ttempt lifecycle); auth/tenancy: client-scoped purchase rows, unchanged; privacy yes (log lines carry ids and allow-listed labels only); health data no; deletion yes (fix round 7: the send fence and the unbound-attempt collector cover the coach as well as the client; fix round 6: finalization also cancels unbound native checkout subscriptions, fail closed); migrations: 20270225000000 and 20270311000000 (additive, down.sql, no user ids); CI gate files no.\n**T3 trigger scan:** n/a (T4).\n**Bounded T1:** none.\n**Canonical builder:** B-RECUR7A-119 (agent 119) for fix round 7; B-RECUR6A-118 (agent 118) for fix round 6; B-RECUR5A-117 (agent 117) for fix round 5; B-RECUR2-116 (agent 116) for fix round 4 content, posted with the restack by B-RECUR3-117 (agent 117); earlier B-RECUR-116 (agent 116), B-RECUR-3 (agent 115), B-RECUR-BE (agent 114).\n**Parent owner:** operator agent 118.\n**Acceptance evidence:** fix round 7 failing-before CI lane [run 37229770060](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37229770060) (5 failed / 8 on 77bce450); after [run 37230098522](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37230098522) (81/81); probe replay [run 37230108455](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37230108455) (incl. real-PostgreSQL fence). fix round 6 failing-before CI lane [run 37220505580](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37220505580) (7 failed / 8 on b04ea692, 1 control passes); after: required checks green at 77bce450 (12 pass, 1 skipping, no reruns); prior-probe replay [run 37220414906](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37220414906). Fix round 5 failing-before CI lane [run 37184276011](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37184276011) (2 failed / 2 on 0c2191c0); after: required checks green at 7252cdb5 and, after the merge-only restack on fees top 13c814f7, at b04ea692 (12 pass, 1 skipping, no reruns). Fix round 4 was a size move plus a merge-only restack on fees top #686 @ e6893c97 (required checks green at 2174eb7c).\n**Promotion triggers:** n/a (already T4).\n\nSplit of #654 (native recurring subscriptions with card-on-file trials, 6,090 lines at `02c48de7`) under the owner's PR size rule: over 3,000 changed lines is an automatic fail (MODEL_ROUTING.md 8.2, tgp-agent-context). #654 is stacked on #627 and was behind #627's head; it was merged with #627 @ `66162285` locally (clean) and cut from that tree. Stack: #627 -> R1 -> R2 -> R3; merge back to back after #627, deploy only after R3 together with mobile #334. Owner adds the Stripe webhook event `setup_intent.succeeded` before that deploy. The tree at R3 equaled the refreshed #654 at the split; since fix round 3 it is #654 plus that round (#654 is superseded). Prior verdicts on #654 (Opus APPROVE 0/0/3 at 02c48de7) do not carry. An unposted Sol draft REQUEST CHANGES 0/3/0 at 02c48de7 (resend after Stripe's 24-hour key window can create a second subscription; error label logging; a failed cancel marks a payable attempt expired) is recorded in tgp-agent-context handoffs/op-115/reports/AUD-SOL-MONEY-115.md and AUD-SOL-MONEY-2-115.md; those findings land in R2/R3; fix round 3 (B-RECUR-116) closes them in R2 (#679) and R3 (#680). Each piece needs fresh Opus 5.5 and Sol audits at its exact head (T4, money path). `tsc --noEmit` passes at every piece. When #627 merges, retarget R1 to main (CodeQL, danger, banned casts and build-sbom then run).\n\n**R1 (this PR, base #627 branch, 2,411 lines after fix round 6; 1,650 after fix round 5):** migrations 20270225000000_native_subscription_trials and 20270311000000_subscription_checkout_terms (+ down.sql), schema, trial-card helper, structured error details in the HTTP exception filter, throttler entry, Stripe Connect API subscription and setup-intent calls, test fakes, Stripe setup doc line. Inert: nothing calls the new checkout code until R2. Live in R1 since fix round 6: account finalization also cancels unbound native checkout subscriptions (none exist before R2) and the plain card update no longer sends `cancel_at_period_end`. Its tests arrive with the callers (R2 http, R3 trial card). Fix round 5: a trial subscription is created with a Stripe-enforced end (`cancel_at_period_end`) that only the attach of the attempt's own saved card lifts (Opus B-679-8 ruling); `isResourceMissing` helper; `test/b-recur5a-117-trial-end-form.spec.ts`.\n\n### Fix rounds\n| Round | Head | Findings | Comment |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1-2 (agents 114/115, on #654) | 795110b7, 02c48de7 | B-654-1..7, C-654-2..4 | [#654 FIX ROUND 2](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/654#issuecomment-5971989117) |\n| 3 (B-RECUR-116) | b89c199d (unchanged) | none open in this piece | [5976055756](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/678#issuecomment-5976055756) |\n| 4 (B-RECUR2-116 content, B-RECUR3-117 restack) | 2174eb7c | size ruling move of inert R2 code into R1 (ebbd170e); restack on #686 @ e6893c97 | [5976827553](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/678#issuecomment-5976827553) |\n| 5 (B-RECUR5A-117) | 7252cdb5 | Opus B-679-8 R1 half (trial created with cancel_at_period_end; the own-card attach lifts it), Opus C-678-1 comment, C-679-3 helper (fix c6c4e74d, test 7252cdb5); dual APPROVE at 0c2191c0 no longer covers this head | [5977577201](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/678#issuecomment-5977577201) |\n| 5 restack (B-RECUR5A-117) | b04ea692 | merge-only onto fees top #686 @ 13c814f7; R1 content unchanged | [5977652920](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/678#issuecomment-5977652920) |\n| 6 (B-RECUR6A-118) | 77bce450 | Opus B-678-2 (plain card update never touches cancel_at_period_end; `liftTrialEnd` on the trial-card attach), #678 